design_tokens.s:
REPO: ~/i/sinc (SvelteKit, already scaffolded + committed). No svelte.config.js exists in this Kit version — all Kit/vite/vitest config lives in vite.config.ts. Global CSS is src/routes/layout.css (imported by src/routes/+layout.svelte). There is NO src/app.css.

CONCEPT (every later step must trace back to this sentence): "sinc is a beat-sync video editor that feels like a hardware sampler — near-black chassis, monospace numerics, one magenta pulse — behaves like a drum machine, and is remembered for the marker rail that flashes on every beat." One accent (beat magenta) + one selection hue (teal). Nothing else is coloured.

1. Fonts. Run exactly:
   mkdir -p static/fonts
   curl -sL -o static/fonts/inter.woff2 "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/inter:vf@latest/latin-wght-normal.woff2"
   curl -sL -o static/fonts/mono.woff2 "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/jetbrains-mono:vf@latest/latin-wght-normal.woff2"
   Verify both files are >30KB (a 404 lands as a tiny HTML file — check with `ls -l static/fonts`).

2. Replace the WHOLE of src/routes/layout.css with:
```css
@import 'tailwindcss';

@font-face {
	font-family: 'Inter';
	src: url('/fonts/inter.woff2') format('woff2-variations');
	font-weight: 100 900;
	font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
	font-family: 'Mono';
	src: url('/fonts/mono.woff2') format('woff2-variations');
	font-weight: 100 800;
	font-display: swap;
}

@theme {
	--color-bg: #0a0a0c;
	--color-panel: #131317;
	--color-panel2: #1b1b21;
	--color-line: #26262e;
	--color-ink: #e9e9ee;
	--color-dim: #85858f;
	--color-beat: #ff2d78;
	--color-sel: #35e0c4;

	--font-sans: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
	--font-mono: 'Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;

	--radius-panel: 10px;
	--ease-snap: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}

html,
body {
	height: 100%;
	overflow: hidden;
	background: var(--color-bg);
	color: var(--color-ink);
	font-family: var(--font-sans);
	-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

button {
	cursor: pointer;
}

:focus-visible {
	outline: 2px solid var(--color-sel);
	outline-offset: 2px;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
	*,
	*::before,
	*::after {
		animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
		transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
	}
}
```
Note: html/body get overflow:hidden because sinc is a fixed-viewport app, never a scrolling page. Individual panels scroll internally.

3. HARD RULE for every later step: no raw colour/px values in .svelte files. Only Tailwind utilities that resolve to the tokens above (bg-panel, text-dim, border-line, text-beat, ring-sel, font-mono, rounded-panel, ease-snap). Positioned overlays (playhead, markers, timeline items) may use inline `style` ONLY for computed geometry (left/width/transform from frame math) — never for colour. All UI text is lowercase.

4. Density direction (the user asked for "compact but roomy"): tight component padding (px-3 py-2), generous gaps between panel groups (gap-3), controls at least 32px tall so they are comfortably clickable, numbers always font-mono with tabular figures.

TESTS (write first, watch fail, then implement, then watch pass — plus `pnpm run check` and `pnpm run lint`):
Create src/lib/tokens.spec.ts (server vitest project — node env, matches src/**/*.{test,spec}.ts):
```ts
import { readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { expect, test } from 'vitest';

const css = readFileSync('src/routes/layout.css', 'utf8');

test('design tokens exist', () => {
	for (const t of [
		'--color-bg', '--color-panel', '--color-panel2', '--color-line',
		'--color-ink', '--color-dim', '--color-beat', '--color-sel',
		'--font-sans', '--font-mono', '--radius-panel', '--ease-snap'
