Dragging (pointerdown / pointermove / pointerup on the item, with setPointerCapture — no library, no dragstart/HTML5 DnD which cannot give smooth pixel deltas):
- pointerdown: ui.sel = x.i; record `grab = { px: e.clientX, p0: x.p, t0: x.t }`.
- pointermove: `const want = grab.p0 + Math.round((e.clientX - grab.px) / ui.zoom)`, then snap, then write x.p (mutate directly for a live preview — do NOT call move_item on every move or the undo stack fills with hundreds of entries).
- pointerup: if x.p !== grab.p0 or the track changed, restore the original values and THEN call move_item(x.i, tid, final) once, so exactly one undo entry lands per drag.
- Vertical: if the pointer is over a different lane of the same kind (video items only over video tracks), retarget the track.

Snapping — put the pure part in src/lib/drop.ts:
```ts
export function drop_pos(
	want: number, len: number, cands: number[], tol_f: number, on: boolean
): number {
	if (!on) return Math.max(0, want);
	const head = snap(want, cands, tol_f);
	if (head !== want) return Math.max(0, head);
	const tail = snap(want + len, cands, tol_f);
	return Math.max(0, tail !== want + len ? tail - len : want);
}
```
Candidates are: 0, every marker p, and every OTHER item's p and p+l. Tolerance in frames is `Math.max(1, Math.round(8 / ui.zoom))` — 8 screen pixels regardless of zoom, which is what makes snapping feel the same when zoomed way in. The head is tried before the tail so a clip's START lands on the beat; that is the actual editing intent and it must not be reversed.

Zoom & scroll on the lane container:
```ts
function wheel(e: WheelEvent) {
	e.preventDefault();
	if (e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) {
		const at = f_of(e.offsetX);                                  // keep the frame under the cursor fixed
		ui.zoom = Math.min(40, Math.max(0.25, ui.zoom * (e.deltaY < 0 ? 1.15 : 1 / 1.15)));
		ui.scroll = Math.max(0, at - e.offsetX / ui.zoom);
	} else {
		ui.scroll = Math.max(0, ui.scroll + (e.deltaX || e.deltaY) / ui.zoom);
	}
}
```
Attach it with `onwheel` on the element; Svelte 5 attaches non-passive listeners for onwheel so preventDefault works.

