$effect(() => {
	JSON.stringify(p);            // touch every field so the effect tracks the whole project
	clearTimeout(t);
	t = setTimeout(save, 800);
});

$effect(() => {
	void restore();
	return () => clearTimeout(t);
});
```
The 800ms debounce exists because a drag mutates p.x on every pointermove; without it every drag would queue dozens of IndexedDB writes. The restore effect must be declared AFTER the autosave effect but is guarded by the fact that restore() only runs once on mount — if it races, the first autosave simply rewrites identical data.

