PHASE 2 — wire transcription into sinc.

1. src/lib/transcribe.ts:
```ts
import { PUBLIC_MS_URL } from '$env/static/public';
import { files } from './media';
import { commit, p } from './project.svelte';
import { sec_to_fr } from './time';

export async function transcribe(sid: string) {
	const f = files.get(sid);
	if (!f) return;
	const res = await fetch(PUBLIC_MS_URL, { method: 'POST', body: f });
	if (!res.ok) throw new Error('transcribe failed: ' + res.status);
	const { t } = (await res.json()) as { t: { n: string; o: number[] }[] };
	commit();
	p.m = p.m.filter((m) => !t.some((x) => x.n === m.g)); // re-runs replace, never duplicate
	for (const x of t)
		for (const o of x.o) p.m.push({ p: sec_to_fr(o, p.f), g: x.n });
	p.m.sort((a, b) => a.p - b.p);
}
```
One commit() for the whole import so undo removes the entire transcription in one press — that matters, because a bad transcription can add hundreds of markers.

2. UI: a "detect" button on every audio (and video-with-audio) source row in the library. While in flight, the row shows an indeterminate bar in bg-beat; on error, the message in text-beat.

3. The marker rail from the markers step already renders one row per group with its name, so instrument groups appear automatically. Add to it:
   - per-group visibility toggle (a `Set<string>` of hidden groups in ui) so a 12-instrument transcription can be collapsed to just the kick
   - group rows use bg-beat at 40% opacity while the hand-tap ('') row stays full strength — the user's own taps must always read as the primary layer
   - a per-group "snap all clips" action: for every timeline item on a video track, move its start to the nearest marker in that group within 12 frames. Route it through move_item so it lands as ONE undoable action (wrap the loop in a single commit() and mutate directly, as the drag handler does).

4. Keep the rail from becoming a wall of pink: cap rendered markers per group to those inside the visible frame range (ui.scroll .. ui.scroll + lane_width / ui.zoom). At 3 minutes and 12 instruments this is the difference between a smooth rail and a stalled browser.

